# chezmoi:managed — edit via 'chezmoi edit' or in ~/git/harmon-dotfiles; direct edits are overwritten by the next 'chezmoi apply' unless re-added
#
# ENVIRONMENT git config for this host — the GitHub transport/credential policy
# (ADR 0002). Personal git config (identity, aliases, diff/merge tools) stays in
# ~/.gitconfig; this file holds only what belongs to the machine.
#
# Why not ~/.gitconfig (issue #42, harmon-init#542): VS Code Dev Containers
# copies ONLY ~/.gitconfig into a container on startup
# (`dev.containers.copyGitConfig`). A macOS-rendered absolute gh path landing in
# a Linux container breaks every remote op (`/opt/homebrew/bin/gh: not found`),
# and the empty `helper =` reset below would discard the credential helper the
# devcontainer deliberately installed. Nothing copies this XDG file, so the
# container keeps its own ~/.config/git/config from the harmon-init image.
#
# Precedence is unchanged by living here: git reads system →
# ~/.config/git/config → ~/.gitconfig, so this file still comes AFTER Homebrew's
# /opt/homebrew/etc/gitconfig (the empty `helper =` still overrides its
# osxkeychain helper) and BEFORE the [includeIf] work-directory sections in
# ~/.gitconfig (which therefore still expand later and can still override the
# helper — the ADR's multi-account escape hatch).
#
# Git only reads this path while XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset or empty; nothing in
# these dotfiles sets it. If that ever changes, this file has to move with it.
{{ $gh := lookPath "gh" -}}
{{ $ghReady := eq (output "sh" "-c" "command -v gh >/dev/null 2>&1 && gh auth status --hostname github.com >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo yes || echo no" | trim) "yes" -}}
{{ if and $gh $ghReady -}}
# GitHub git operations go over HTTPS, authenticated by gh's token (ADR 0002,
# issue #37) — pushes never depend on the SSH agent being unlocked. Do NOT run
# `gh auth setup-git` on machines managed by these dotfiles — it writes
# ~/.gitconfig, and `git config --global` does too; both are read after this
# file and would shadow it.
#
# Rendered only when gh is installed AND authenticated (checked at apply
# time): on a freshly provisioned machine before `gh auth login`, this block
# is omitted entirely so existing SSH pushes keep working — the policy
# activates on the first apply after login and degrades back if auth is lost.
[credential "https://github.com"]
	helper =
	helper = !{{ $gh }} auth git-credential
[credential "https://gist.github.com"]
	helper =
	helper = !{{ $gh }} auth git-credential
# Rewrite every GitHub SSH URL form to HTTPS for fetch AND push — the scp
# form (git@github.com:) plus all three ssh:// forms, including the explicit
# port-443 endpoint — so legacy SSH remotes, submodules, and SSH-form clone
# URLs transparently use the gh credential helper. Pushes still go through
# the named remote, so tracking refs update normally (pushing to a raw HTTPS
# URL is what caused the stale "ahead 1").
[url "https://github.com/"]
	insteadOf = git@github.com:
	insteadOf = ssh://git@github.com/
	insteadOf = ssh://git@ssh.github.com:443/
	insteadOf = ssh://git@ssh.github.com/
[url "https://gist.github.com/"]
	insteadOf = git@gist.github.com:
	insteadOf = ssh://git@gist.github.com/
{{- end }}
